---
import { docsHref } from "../lib/site";

const workflows = [
  { title: "Delegate the outcome.", text: "Give a Crew lead the job, constraints, and what done means. It assigns work to visible mission workers.", href: "/distros#included-distros", link: "Set up your crew" },
  { title: "Unblock the work.", text: "See who is working and who needs a decision. Answer the blocker, not every step along the way.", href: "/agents", link: "See agent attention" },
  { title: "Review the result.", text: "Inspect the diff, checks, and review threads. Send precise feedback back to the agent.", href: "/agents#driving-an-agent-in-a-pane", link: "Steer agent work" },
];
---
<section class="workflow-proof" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
  <div class="agent-fit">
    <p>Your agents are the workforce.</p>
    <p class="agent-names">Claude Code <span>·</span> Codex <span>·</span> fx <span>·</span> OpenCode <span>·</span> pi <span>·</span> Oh My Pi <span>·</span> Grok</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/agents#agent-setup")}>Integrations, MCP, and any CLI agent <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <header><p class="eyebrow">Delegate. Supervise. Unblock. Review.</p><h2 id="workflow-title">Give it the job.<br />Get the work back.</h2></header>
  <div class="workflow-grid">
    {workflows.map((workflow, index) => (
      <article>
        <span class="step" aria-hidden="true">0{index + 1}</span>
        <h3>{workflow.title}</h3>
        <p>{workflow.text}</p>
        <a href={docsHref(workflow.href)}>{workflow.link} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="boundary">Work continues while the server stays up. A server crash or machine reboot ends running programs.</p>
</section>

<details class="control-proof">
  <summary>The tools behind agent work <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
  <div class="control-content">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Agents execute. You make the calls.</p>
    <h2 id="control-title">Stop polling tabs.<br />Wait for what matters.</h2>
    <p>Agents inspect state, wait for changes, and hand work to each other through the same tools. You see the work in flight, answer the decisions that need you, and review the result.</p>
    <p>Need to step in? <code>phux take @7</code> gives you exclusive input. Automation cannot type into a pane you hold. Release it with <code>phux give @7</code>.</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/agents#driving-an-agent-in-a-pane")}>The agent control loop <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <figure>
    <figcaption>Tools your agents use · an example, not a live feed</figcaption>
    <pre><code><span># See who is doing what</span>{"\n"}phux agent list{"\n\n"}<span># Wait for the next agent that needs you</span>{"\n"}phux agent wait --any --until blocked --timeout 600{"\n\n"}<span># Inspect its pane before sending input</span>{"\n"}phux snapshot @7{"\n\n"}<span># Send a follow-up to that exact agent</span>{"\n"}phux agent prompt @7 'Run the tests again'</code></pre>
    <p>Use the pane returned by your own agent list. A wait observes a new transition; a delivery receipt is not proof the work is finished.</p>
  </figure>
  </div>
</details>

<section class="product-fit" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Crew · first-party agent orchestration</p>
    <h2 id="fit-title">One lead.<br />A visible crew.</h2>
    <p>Give a lead agent the outcome. With Crew, it places workers in isolated Git worktrees and visible panes, supervises their missions, checks their evidence, and brings back the result.</p>
    <a href={docsHref("/distros#included-distros")}>Set up Crew <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    <p class="crew-requirements">Crew requires a phux source checkout, a build with native missions, Python 3.9+, and configured agents. It is coordination, not a security sandbox or a promise of unattended completion.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="mission-brief">
    <figcaption>Example task for a configured Crew lead</figcaption>
    <blockquote>Fix the flaky checkout test. Open a PR. Don’t merge it.</blockquote>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Delegate</strong><span>Workers get their own worktrees and visible panes.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Unblock</strong><span>Questions and permission prompts still come to you.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Review</strong><span>The lead checks the evidence and brings back the result.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </figure>
</section>

<style>
  section, .control-proof { margin-top: 72px; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding-top: 48px; }
  h2 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: clamp(30px, 3.5vw, 44px); line-height: 1.12; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: 23px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.035em; }
  p { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
  a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: 44px; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: 13px; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 4px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 12px; }
  .agent-fit { margin-bottom: 64px; text-align: center; }
  .agent-fit > p:first-child { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .agent-names { margin: 0; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 19px); line-height: 1.8; }
  .agent-names span { padding-inline: 8px; color: var(--color-dim); }
  .agent-fit a { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .workflow-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 48px 40px; margin-top: 40px; }
  article { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: start; min-width: 0; }
  .step { margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--color-dim); font: 12px var(--font-code); }
  article p { margin: 14px 0 18px; }
  article a { margin-top: auto; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .boundary { margin: 24px 0 0; max-width: 100ch; color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 12px; }
  .control-content, .product-fit { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: center; }
  .control-content > div > p:not(.eyebrow), .product-fit > div > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 48ch; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
  .control-proof { padding-top: 16px; }
  .control-proof > summary { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; color: var(--color-muted); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; font-size: 13px; }
  .control-proof > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .control-proof[open] > summary > span { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  .control-content { padding-top: 24px; }
  figure { min-width: 0; margin: 0; padding: 24px; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius: 10px; }
  figcaption, figure p { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; }
  pre { margin: 24px 0; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-fg); }
  pre span { color: var(--color-muted); }
  figure p { margin: 0; }
  blockquote { margin: 24px 0; color: var(--color-fg); font-size: clamp(22px, 2.5vw, 30px); line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .mission-brief ol { display: grid; gap: 18px; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .mission-brief li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 76px 1fr; gap: 12px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .mission-brief strong { color: var(--color-fg); font-weight: 500; }
  .mission-brief li span { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .product-fit > div > .crew-requirements { color: var(--color-dim); font-size: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .workflow-grid { gap: 28px; } .control-content, .product-fit { gap: 28px; } }
  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    section { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 32px; }
    .agent-fit { text-align: left; margin-bottom: 40px; }
    .agent-names span { padding-inline: 3px; }
    .workflow-grid, .control-content, .product-fit { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .workflow-grid { gap: 28px; margin-top: 32px; }
    article { padding-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
    article h3 { font-size: 25px; }
    .step { margin-bottom: 10px; }
    article p { margin-block: 12px; }
    figure { padding: 20px; }
  }
</style>
